\v 17 and¦124921 she¦124921 also said¦124921, “He¦124926 gave¦124926 me¦124927 all this barley¦124924 because¦124928 he¦124929 told¦124929 me that he didn't¦124931 want me to return¦124933 to¦124935 my mother-in-law¦124937 empty-handed¦124934.”
\p
\v 18 “\add Okay\add* my¦124941 daughter¦124941,” \add @Naomi¦124941\add* responded¦124939. “Wait \add now\add* until¦124942 we see¦124944 what happens¦124946, because¦124948 that¦124943 man¦124951 won't¦124949 rest today until the¦124957 matter¦124957 gets settled.”
\c 4
\s1 Boaz takes over the land and gets Ruth as a wife
\rem /s1 Boaz Marries Ruth; The Marriage of Boaz and Ruth
\p
\v 1 \add Meanwhile,\add* Boaz¦124960 went¦124961 to \add the place inside\add* the¦124962 \add town\add* gate¦124962 \add (where people conducted their official business)\add* and¦124963 sat¦124963 down¦124963 there¦124964. Just as he had hoped, the¦124966 man responsible for Naomi's family came along¦124967—the man whom¦124968 Boaz¦124971 had mentioned earlier—and¦124972 \add @Boaz¦124972\add* called out to him by name and said¦124972, “Come over here¦124976 and¦124979 sit¦124974 down.” So the man came over and¦124980 sat¦124980 down¦124980.
\v 2 Then¦124982 \add @Boaz¦124982\add* called over ten¦124983 of¦124985 the¦124985 older, well-respected men¦124984 from the¦124986 town¦124986 and¦124987 asked¦124987 them to sit¦124988 \add and witness their discussion\add*, so¦124991 they¦124991 sat¦124991 down¦124991 \add with them\add*.
\v 3 Then¦124993 \add @Boaz¦124993\add* asked¦124993 the other relative, “The part¦124995 of¦124995 the¦124996 countryside¦124996 that¦124997 belonged¦124998 to¦124998 our¦124998 relative Elimelek¦124999 is for sale. Naomi¦125001, who¦125002 \add recently\add* returned¦125002 from¦125003 Moab¦125004, is selling¦125000 it.
\v 4 I thought that¦125027 I should tell¦125025 you \add about it\add* and¦125014 \add in case\add* you buy \add the land\add* while the people sitting¦125013 here are listening, including these leaders¦125015 of¦125015 our people¦125016. If¦125017 you¦125019 want to \add ≈buy it back into the family\add*, then¦125021 do so¦125027. But if¦125021 you do not¦125023 want to¦125026 \add ≈buy it back\add*, then let me¦125026 know¦125027, because¦125029 you¦125031 are the closest relative to¦125032 Elimelek, and¦125033 I¦125033 am¦125034 next after¦125034 you¦125034.”
\p “I'll buy it¦125035,” the man replied¦125035.
\p
\v 5 “When¦125039 you¦125043 buy the¦125044 land from¦125045 Naomi¦125046,” Boaz¦125040 continued¦125039, “you will also¦125047 need to marry Ruth¦125048, our deceased relative's widow from Moab, so that she'll have¦125053 a son who \add ≈will inherit¦125061\add* the property and continue Elimelek's family line.”
\p
\v 6 “I can't buy it¦125063 back myself, then,” the¦125064 closer relative answered¦125063. “If I¦125066 did that, I¦125073 would ruin¦125073 my¦125076 own¦125076 son's inheritance¦125076. You¦125080 can have the land and the woman instead of¦125083 me, because¦125084 I¦125087 \add simply\add* can't take it.”
\p
\v 7 (At that¦125090 \add #time¦125091\add* in¦125092 Yisrael¦125092, people had a different way of buying \add land\add* or exchanging¦125098 \add goods between them\add*. In order to make these \add #matters¦125102\add* legally binding, one man would take off¦125103 one of¦125105 his¦125105 \add #sandals¦125105\add* and¦125106 give¦125106 it¦125106 to¦125107 the other party. That¦125108 was¦125109 the¦125109 way people in¦125110 Yisrael¦125110 confirmed¦125099 what they had agreed to do.)\x + \xo 4:7-8: \xt Deu 25:9.\x*
\p
\v 8 “You buy it¦125112 yourself,” the relative said¦125112 and¦125118 he¦125118 took off¦125118 one of¦125119 his¦125119 \add #sandals¦125119\add* \add and gave it to Boaz\add*.
\v 9 Then¦125121 Boaz¦125122 said¦125121 to¦125123 the respected men and¦125124 to all¦125124 the¦125126 other people¦125126 who were¦125127 there, “Today you¦125128 have all witnessed¦125127 that¦125130 I've¦125131 bought from¦125144 Naomi¦125145 all¦125134 the property that¦125136 belonged¦125137 to¦125137 Elimelek¦125137, Kilion¦125142, and¦125143 Mahlon¦125143.
\v 10 I am also¦125147 taking Ruth¦125150, Mahlon's¦125153 widow from Moab, to be my wife¦125152 so that she can have a¦125156 son. Everyone will consider that son to¦125157 be Elimelek's descendant and he \add ≈will inherit¦125163\add* the property and carry on Elimelek's family name¦125167 among his relatives¦125171 and¦125172 here in his¦125173 hometown.\x + \xo 4:10: \xt Deu 25:5-6.\x* You've¦125175 seen and heard that today \add and can tell anyone who asks about it\add*.”
\p
\v 11 All¦125179 the¦125181 respected men¦125181, and the others who were¦125184 sitting at¦125184 the \add town\add* gate¦125184, agreed, and¦125185 they said¦125178, “Yes, \add we are your\add*. We¦125186 pray that¦125182 Yahweh¦125188 will allow this woman¦125191 who¦125192 will be¦125192 coming¦125192 into¦125193 your¦125195 home, to be like¦125196 Rahel¦125196 \add !(Rachel¦125196)\add* and¦125198 Leah¦125198, the¦125201 two¦125201 who gave birth to our ancestors and started our people¦125181, Yisrael¦125205.\x + \xo 4:11: \xt Gen 29:31.\x* May you become great in¦125209 the clan of Efratah¦125209 and¦125210 famous here in¦125213 Beyt-Lehem¦125214!
\v 12 We pray that your¦125217 family will be¦125216 like¦125218 the¦125218 family¦125218 of¦125218 \add your ancestor\add* Perez¦125219, son of Judah¦125224 and Tamar¦125223, because of the¦125227 many descendants¦125227 that¦125228 Yahweh¦125230 will¦125229 give¦125229 to¦125231 you and this¦125235 young¦125234 woman¦125234.”\x + \xo 4:12: \xt Gen 38:27-30.\x*
\s1 Boaz' descendants
\rem /s1 The Genealogy of David; The Descendants of Boaz; Boaz and His Descendants
\p
\v 13 \add ≈So¦125237\add* Boaz¦125238 married Ruth¦125241, and¦125246 \add when\add* he¦125246 \add ≈slept with\add* her¦125247, Yahweh¦125249 enabled her to \add ≈become¦125242 pregnant\add* and¦125252 she¦125252 gave¦125252 birth¦125252 to a¦125253 son¦125253.
\v 14 The¦125256 women¦125256 \add in Beyt-Lehem\add* said¦125255 to¦125257 Naomi¦125259, “Praise Yahweh¦125261 for¦125265 giving you¦125265 a¦125266 \add male descendant\add* to preserve your family today. \add We pray to Yahweh that people throughout\add* Yisrael¦125270 will greatly respect him.
\v 15 ⇔Your¦125281 daughter-in-law¦125281, who¦125282 loves¦125284 you¦125284 and who's¦125286 been¦125289 better¦125289 to¦125290 you¦125290 than¦125291 if¦125280 you had seven¦125291 sons¦125292, has given¦125285 birth¦125285 to¦125285 him. Now he'll make you feel young again and he'll \add ≈take care of\add* you when you get old¦125279.”
\v 16 Then¦125294 Naomi¦125295 picked¦125294 up the¦125298 baby¦125298 and¦125299 held him¦125299 closely and¦125301 became¦125301 like second mother to¦125303 him¦125303.
\p
\v 17 The¦125308 women who were living nearby said¦125310, “It is as if Naomi¦125314 now has¦125311 a¦125313 son¦125313!” They¦125315 named¦125316 him Obed¦125317.
\rem /s1 The ancestry of David
\p \add Eventually\add* \add @Obed¦125318\add* went on to become the¦125319 father¦125319 of¦125319 Yishay¦125321 \add !(Jesse¦125321)\add*, who became the¦125322 father¦125322 of¦125322 \add King\add* David¦125323.
\v 18 Here is¦125327 a list of the¦125327 descendants¦125327 of¦125327 Perez¦125328: Perez's¦125329 son was Hezron¦125333.
\v 19 Hezron's¦125335 son was Ram¦125339 and¦125340 Ram's¦125340 son was Amminadab¦125344.
\v 20 Amminadab's¦125346 son was Nahshon¦125350 and¦125351 Nahshon's¦125351 son was Salmon.
\v 21 Salmon's¦125357 son was Boaz¦125361 and¦125362 Boaz's¦125362 son was Obed¦125366.
\v 22 Obed's¦125368 son was Yishay¦125372 \add !(Jesse¦125372)\add* and¦125373 Yishay's¦125373 son was \add King\add* David¦125377.
